{
 "command": "dialog-benchmark-layout",
 "notes": [
  "Feeds W8-18r (dialogs::benchmark::{layout, state}). Reflection over the internal BenchmarkDialog of the PhotoReview (Shell.Win32) assembly, the public BenchmarkResultRow / BenchmarkPresenter of PhotoReview.App.Shared and the public BenchmarkProfiles / BenchmarkPhaseResult of PhotoReview.Benchmarking; no window is created. The language is the process default (English).",
  "Output per kind: dialog -> title, items [{class, id, text, style, ex_style}], initial_focus_id, default_button_id, resizable, header_ids, uses_modal_frame, extra_window_style, initial_folder_text (only when initial_folder is not null); column_headers -> headers[10]; compare_rows -> sign (-1, 0, 1); sort_clicks -> states [[column, direction]] after each click; preferred -> preferred_width, preferred_height, minimum_width, minimum_height; metrics -> margin, field_height, button_height; constants -> the 19 control ids and column_count.",
  "compare_rows: rows are built from the baseline registry (profile_id) and a phase (workload, samples, status). The text columns use pairs that differ in their first letter so the sign does not depend on the machine's collation; the Rust test passes an ordinal comparer for those columns, and the culture comparer (CompareStringEx) is covered by a separate native test. Empty samples give 0 for every percentile.",
  "preferred and metrics use a window-less dialog (RuntimeHelpers.GetUninitializedObject with _avgCharWidth, _lineHeight, _childHosts set), so ButtonWidth is exactly Dx(50) and every measured height is 0. sort_clicks calls SortBy on a real dialog without a window: the grid and the header are absent, so only the (column, direction) state changes."
 ],
